# Line endings.
#
# This project is developed on macOS and gated on the windows-latest CI runner,
# where git's core.autocrlf=true rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. That is
# not cosmetic: CRLF moves `#!/usr/bin/env node` off line 1, and any tool that
# re-emits the file (Vite's SSR transform, which Vitest runs project .mjs through
# by default) then produces a module that cannot be parsed at all — the suite
# fails to LOAD with a bare `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token` and no
# location. That is exactly how the 3.3.6 release gate went red on Windows.
#
# Pinning these to LF makes the bytes identical on every platform, so no tooling
# decision depends on how a developer's machine happened to configure git.
#
# Deliberately scoped rather than `* text=auto`: only files that carry a shebang
# or are executed by a shell need a fixed ending, and a repo-wide rule would
# rewrite checkouts (and fixtures that may legitimately contain CRLF) for no gain.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
